sequenceDiagram
    participant C as Client
    participant A as Auctions - PlaceBidCommandHandler
    participant ADB as Auctions tables
    participant AOP as Auctions OutboxProcessor
    participant W as Wallets - BidPlacedEventHandler
    participant WDB as Wallets tables

    C->>A: POST /api/auctions/{id}/bid {amount} with a JWT
    A->>ADB: GetAuctionByIdAsync (tracked entity)
    A->>A: Auction.ApplyNewBid: Active, not ended, Amount above CurrentPrice, not the seller, not the current winner
    A->>A: EndsOn += 30 s when less than AntiSnipingWindow remains, new Version
    A->>ADB: UPDATE Auctions + OutboxMessages(BidPlacedEvent) in one SaveChangesAsync
    alt Version conflict with AuctionCloser
        A-->>C: 409 {error: Data corrupted, try again}
    else saved
        A-->>C: 200
    end
    AOP->>W: Publish(BidPlacedEvent) on the next poll
    W->>WDB: WasEventProcessedAsync(EventId)
    W->>W: new winner: Wallet.LockFunds(NewPrice)
    W->>W: previous winner: Wallet.UnlockFunds(PreviousPrice), only when PreviousWinningUserId is set
    W->>WDB: UPDATE Wallets + WalletsProcessedMessages with CancellationToken.None
    alt InsufficientFundsException
        W--xAOP: handler throws: FailedAttempt, retry after 20 / 40 / 80 / 160 s, dead after the 5th failure
        Note over A,W: the auction keeps the new leader although no funds were locked
    end
